add('ig',1,'A refusal can be an informative contribution','Test the working hunch that a refusal sometimes improves the next conversational step instead of counting only continued participation.','The refusal-as-information hunch is plausible from the constructed dialogues, but its general interpersonal effect has not been established.', '''Intuition, stated precisely: “A refusal can carry useful information for choosing the next conversational step.” Strength is moderate as a working pattern. Trigger: the different refusal branches in the constructed reading-group cases. Experience source is visible case reasoning, not a claimed human lifetime or expert-hour count. The original’s 10,000-hour weighting heuristic is not used as evidence of this assistant’s expertise.

Five bias checks: familiarity—the already used permission framing could predetermine the answer; fear—no bodily fear is asserted; sunk cost—prior writing gives no new evidence; confirmation—the broad program could tempt every output to become a KEEP; status quo—an alternative fixed encouragement script must remain a concrete comparator. Each is a possible evaluation failure, not a diagnosis of a person.

What would be true if the intuition is right? At least one refusal contains a condition that changes an appropriate next question or stop decision. Evidence sought: the explicit words in three constructed replies. “The hour is fine; required homework is not” identifies obligation, “raw notes not public; finalized excerpt okay” identifies representation scope, and “I do not want to discuss it” identifies a stop. They yield different next operations. Human comfort, increased interest and renewed participation are not part of this finite demonstration.

→ /ar 8x invoked in dependency-ig-1-ar.md and .json. The original execution has forty-six numbered claims; root and every nonterminal have three children; one path reaches seven recursive edges; other branches reach five. It records exact assumptions, costs, foreclosures and three actual generated transcript outputs. Possible causal or interpretive extensions remain conditional. The source and requirements receipt are separate.

Underlying pattern: a negative response is not a single semantic class. It can reject a condition, limit a scope, decline an entire activity, or end discussion. Making that implicit distinction explicit changes the available next operations. A refusal without a reason does not permit inventing one.

Eight probes: “not today” leaves other times open but unpromised; “not publicly” limits audience; “not with mandatory homework” limits obligation; “not this topic” limits content; “not with my name” limits attribution but may not permit anonymous use; “not unless I can preview it” creates a prerequisite; “not at all” ends the offer; “I do not want to discuss why” ends the reason inquiry. These are constructed language cases, not predictions about hidden motives.

Action: convert the locally supported intuition into the explicit task “classify the stated refusal scope before generating a next question.” The goal remains broad voluntary inquiry; no refusal is required to become agreement. The local claim is validated by the produced distinctions, so /exd is not required for this finite semantic claim. The broader hypothesis that this improves human relationships remains unverified and is not bundled into that validation.

Later application: generated next step for “not publicly” is “Would a private version fit?” only when the original invitation remains open; for “not at all,” the next step is an acknowledgment and stop. This repeats distinctions already credited in social and listening work, so the intuition procedure earns no additional KEEP.

Certificate: the specific replies contain different explicit restrictions and yield different generated next operations. That establishes the modal local claim; it does not establish a general human effect or a new independent benefit beyond prior uptake.''','The hunch is supported as a finite semantic distinction and converted into a local response goal; broader interpersonal benefit remains untested.','The generated next-step choice follows the actual scope of each constructed refusal.','UNRESOLVED','Content keeps the modest local claim separate from a causal relationship hypothesis. Organization links all AR nodes and live outputs; repeated adoption receives no additional credit.','Test an ambiguous refusal without a stated condition; compare actual recipient confirmation if available; examine a refusal that invites no further question.',N+' Five intuition steps, five bias checks, eight probes and required AR dependency at its explicit 8x floors.')
add('ig',2,'A tiny start might change motivation in either direction','Test the hunch that a voluntary gateway can increase inquiry starts without reducing inherent interest.','A two-minute self-chosen entry appears promising, but I do not know whether it increases meaningful starts, substitutes tracking for inquiry, or adds unwanted obligation.', '''Intuition: “A self-chosen two-minute gateway can increase voluntary starts without reducing intrinsic interest.” Working strength moderate. Trigger: the constructed habit designs distinguish preparation, substantive inquiry and interest. No bodily feeling, personal history or human expertise-hour total is attributed to the assistant.

Bias checks: familiarity—the two-minute form is recognizable and could receive unearned confidence; fear—the case has no evidence of fear of a larger task; sunk cost—the already written habit plans do not prove effectiveness; confirmation—the program’s desire for change can bias against a null result; status quo—the no-gateway voluntary control is a serious alternative. Domain track record for this exact intervention is unavailable.

Predictions if right: some eligible setting has more substantive starts and no reduction in intrinsic interest. Counter-patterns: more document openings without examples; more starts with less interest; equal starts with extra tracking; fewer self-chosen sessions because the routine feels imposed. These are possible causal accounts to distinguish, not observed outcomes.

→ /ar 8x invoked in dependency-ig-2-ar.md and .json. Forty-six claims, three children at every nonterminal, seven recursive edges on the longest branch, and explicit costs/foreclosures are retained. Human causal tests are BEDROCK-TEST-DEFERRED because there are no participants or outcome data. The actual local event classifications are labeled as such, not as causal tests.

Underlying-pattern candidate: a small concrete example may lower entry demands while preserving a chosen question. Alternative pattern: the gateway becomes an external completion target and displaces intrinsic inquiry. The original reward research contains differing effects by reward form, so an assumed general motivational boost from completion is not justified. [Deci, original experiments](https://davidjoannes.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/Effects-of-Externally-Mediated-Rewards-On-Intrinsic-Motivation-Edward-Deci.pdf)

Eight discriminating dimensions: optional versus required; same versus newly attractive question; preparation versus substantive example; initiation versus continuation; inherent interest versus completion satisfaction; actual access versus offered opportunity; chosen stop versus failure; short-run response versus lasting habit. None is settled by calling the practice small.

Action: intuition plausible but unverified → /exd invoked in dependency-ig-2-exd.md, with actual power arithmetic in dependency-ig-2-exd-power.json. That full original design specifies hypotheses, variables, parallel randomization, active control, twenty validity threats, provisional sample assumptions and a fixed analysis plan. It preserves both conjuncts: more starts alone does not pass, and nonsignificant interest change does not prove no reduction. The normal-approximation planning total is 794 under explicit assumed effects/variance and attrition; this is not a recruitment action or a validated achieved-power claim.

Later application: mock event “opened the question but wrote no example” is classified as preparation, while “accessible opportunity declined” is a decline and “example written” is a substantive start. This prevents proxy confusion in the design but does not show that a human’s motivation changed.

Certificate: no human outcome discriminates the positive gateway mechanism from displacement or unwanted-obligation mechanisms. The available classification and design work is complete; the causal intuition remains unresolved. A real trial or other appropriate direct evidence would be needed for the human claim.''','The intuition remains a plausible competing causal hypothesis; its test now measures the intended conjunction and preserves null or adverse outcomes.','The proposed experiment cannot manufacture success from starts alone or a failure to detect interest loss.','UNRESOLVED','Content separates local measurement validity from unobserved causal effectiveness. Organization retains the AR registry, experiment design and power assumptions without counting them as human execution.','Pilot actual interest and work-product measures if a real study is undertaken; compare a different gateway; test whether voluntary stopping itself changes the appropriate success criterion.',N+' Five intuition steps, eight discriminating dimensions, required AR at its explicit 8x floors and full EXD design; human causal trial is unperformed.')
